Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Enables the USB power settings in the control panel
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Power\PowerSettings\2a737441-1930-4402-8d77-b2bebba308a3\48e6b7a6-50f5-4782-a5d4-53bb8f07e226]
"Attributes"=dword:00000002

; These settings can be found under:
; Control Panel -> Hardware and Sound -> Power Options -> Change plan settings -> Change advanced power settings

; Two settings to change that might affect the Mouse Trapper scrolling behavior:
; 1. USB selective suspend setting (in advanced power settings) - disable!
; 2. Device manager -> Universal Serial Bus Controllers -> USB Root Hub (probably more than one, change for all of them)
;    -> properties -> Power Management tab -> uncheck "Allow the computer to turn off this device to save power"
